#X text 870 690 Volume (it turns DSP on - start low). A clear bell = its best move. A dull pluck = a random move: it is exploring. A chord = it reached the goal., f 56;
#N canvas 40 60 1250 1320 one-move 0;
#X text 20 10 ONE MOVE of the agent: [r \$0-move] gets one bang per tick of the clock (or per step of practice). The table Q is the array q\$0: the value of move a on note s is q\$0[4 * s + a] \, with a = 0 1 2 3 = 2 down \, 1 down \, 1 up \, 2 up. A [t b b ...] fires from right to left: read it from its right outlet., f 170;
#X obj 1000 70 array define q\$0 32;
#X text 1000 96 <- the table: 8 notes x 4 moves, f 22;
#N canvas 40 60 700 620 values 0;
#X text 20 10 The [value]s the agent reads and writes inside [expr] (an [expr] can only assign to a [value] that exists). The _\$0 makes them private to this copy of the lesson., f 90;
#X obj 20 60 v s_\$0;
#X text 140 60 the note it is on (the state), f 60;
#X obj 20 87 v a_\$0;
#X text 140 87 the move it chose (the action), f 60;
#X obj 20 114 v s2_\$0;
#X text 140 114 the next note, f 60;
#X obj 20 141 v r_\$0;
#X text 140 141 the reward of the move, f 60;
#X obj 20 168 v dn_\$0;
#X text 140 168 1 when the phrase is done, f 60;
#X obj 20 195 v dl_\$0;
#X text 140 195 the surprise of the last update, f 60;
#X obj 20 222 v ex_\$0;
#X text 140 222 1 = this move was random (exploring), f 60;
#X obj 20 249 v o_\$0;
#X text 140 249 where the search for the best move starts, f 60;
#X obj 20 276 v ra_\$0;
#X text 140 276 a random move, f 60;
#X obj 20 303 v m_\$0;
#X text 140 303 the best value on this note, f 60;
#X obj 20 330 v ls_\$0;
#X text 140 330 the last move: its note ..., f 60;
#X obj 20 357 v la_\$0;
#X text 140 357 ... and its move (for good! and bad), f 60;
#X obj 20 384 v n_\$0;
